WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.190 --> 00:00:03.379
STATE OF SONY:
Once upon a time, Sony was one of the largest

00:00:03.379 --> 00:00:05.859
electronics companies in the world.

00:00:05.859 --> 00:00:10.280
They were synonymous with home entertainment,
high quality cameras, and hit movies.

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:17.830
But, the past 20 years haven’t been so kind
to Sony as it’s simply been loss after loss

00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:19.359
after loss.

00:00:19.359 --> 00:00:21.490
Take their TV business for example.

00:00:21.490 --> 00:00:27.690
Up until 2006, Sony was the world’s number
1 TV manufacturer, a title that they had held

00:00:27.690 --> 00:00:29.010
for decades.

00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:32.820
But, since then, it’s been the Samsung show.

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:37.840
In fact, Samsung has now held this title for
17 years themselves.

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:42.870
Sony didn’t just lose their dominant position
either, they straight up got sidelined.

00:00:42.870 --> 00:00:49.350
In fact, Sony currently stands at 5th place
within the TV market beaten by Samsung, Vizio,

00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:53.550
LG, and TCL with only 6% market share.

00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:57.950
Things were going so bad that Sony actually
decided to spin off their TV business after

00:00:57.950 --> 00:00:59.890
10 years of losses.

00:00:59.890 --> 00:01:04.309
But, it’s not just legacy businesses in
which Sony has been getting burned.

00:01:04.309 --> 00:01:09.820
They’ve had quite a bit of trouble entering
new industries as well such as the computer

00:01:09.820 --> 00:01:10.820
industry.

00:01:10.820 --> 00:01:14.450
After failing to break into the PC industry
for years, Sony would end up selling off their

00:01:14.450 --> 00:01:15.700
PC business.

00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:18.909
A similar story can be seen with their smartphone
efforts as well.

00:01:18.909 --> 00:01:23.009
They haven’t yet quit making smartphones
but for several years now, they haven’t

00:01:23.009 --> 00:01:24.880
even been able to break 1% marketshare globally.

00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:32.300
To be honest, the only Sony segment that’s
still super strong is selling playstations.

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:36.450
Everything else is at best stagnating or slowly
bleeding market share.

00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:41.280
Seeing all this, I don’t think you’d be
surprised to hear that Sony was tens of billions

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:43.229
of dollars during the worst of it.

00:01:43.229 --> 00:01:49.100
But, despite all this, Sony has somehow been
turning this entire situation around.

00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:54.460
After several years of losses, Sony has been
positing consistent profits for 6 years now.

00:01:54.460 --> 00:01:56.780
Their stock graph tells the same story.

00:01:56.780 --> 00:02:02.140
After their peak in 2000, Sony would fall
over 90% over the next 12 years.

00:02:02.140 --> 00:02:06.280
But, since then, they’ve recovered much
of these losses.

00:02:06.280 --> 00:02:08.099
How could this be possible though?

00:02:08.099 --> 00:02:12.349
Sony has been losing ground in basically every
segment that we know them for.

00:02:12.349 --> 00:02:17.629
Well, join me as we take a look back at Sony’s
existential crisis and how they were able

00:02:17.629 --> 00:02:23.810
to come out the otherside profitable.

00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:29.980
STIFF COMPETITION:
Sony’s fall from grace shows how even major

00:02:29.980 --> 00:02:34.800
corporations can falter if they don’t adapt
to changing times.

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:39.099
With high inflation and historically high
interest rates, we’re very much experiencing

00:02:39.099 --> 00:02:41.960
a shift in the investing landscape.

